  "implementation": [
    "A second exact own-data plain active_binding hint becomes pre-admission rate_limited only when it names a different, unique original, same-scope, unattempted account. The operation ends without a third bind, redraw, wait or another winner revalidation.",
    "Known concurrency denial or a strictly validated numeric full snapshot becomes rate_limited during initial selection or the one fresh winner check. Capacity remains advisory until the original fenced lease/admission authority.",
    "Malformed/untyped hints, ambiguous or disallowed scope, CAS/expiry/storage errors, invalid capacity snapshots and unavailable/malformed runtime health remain fail-closed blocks under the existing HTTP 503 mapping. Durable health denial retains precedence; eligibility/window-only exclusion remains account_denied.",
    "New immediate rate limits do not invent Retry-After. Existing optional sticky-wait/degrade behavior, SQL/parameters, roles/grants/schema, funds guards and timeout bounds are unchanged by this repair.",
    "No PG wrapper or Redis release implementation changed. The throwing-release unit case proves behavior for a rejected promise and every attempted temporary release; it does not prove real Redis delivery or network acknowledgement."
  ],
