  "newPostgresCases": [
    {
      "name": "restricted PostgreSQL terminal second affinity contention is rate limited without a third bind",
      "proof": "Three independently connected restricted gateway actors: A commits an empty affinity read; B binds P; A receives the real typed P conflict. Actual PG leases fill P, C performs capacity-driven stale invalidation and binds Q, then leases release so A freshly revalidates P. A second real bind receives Q contention and returns rate_limited with two A binds, one fresh winner check and no third bind. Both losing proposals preserve full timestamps/TTL/revision/fence."
    },
    {
      "name": "restricted PostgreSQL fresh affinity winner capacity is rate limited without a second bind",
      "proof": "Actual restricted-role PG leases fill P after A receives its first typed hint. Fresh eligibility/health reads still succeed, the actual PG concurrency read reports two held leases, and A returns rate_limited with no second bind or affinity mutation."
    },
    {
      "name": "restricted PostgreSQL initially full candidate capacity is rate limited without any bind",
      "proof": "Actual PG leases fill both original accounts before selection. Real eligibility/health/concurrency reads yield a capacity rate limit without any affinity resolve or bind."
    }
  ],
  "evidenceBoundaries": [
    "Both versions ran the same five-case component root; each logged 5/5 with zero skips. Their 686-file literal-relative-import/runner/roles/package-lock closures match before, after and projection creation. This is not a whole-repository or future freeze.",
    "Production operations use restricted gateway roles. Migrator access is fixture setup and observer-only full timestamp/financial reads; no new grants, superuser shortcuts, schema or timeout changes.",
    "Passed assertions compare nine existing synthetic fixture financial/request table count-and-digest snapshots before/after. They prove these component operations leave fixture rows unchanged; no separate financial receipt or HTTP settlement/refund result is asserted.",
    "Redis is an in-memory slot bookkeeping double in these component cases. Zero tracked slots and exact release calls do not prove real Redis network acknowledgement.",
    "These are local functional component and offline checks, not HTTP/provider/admission end-to-end acceptance, durability/performance measurements, formal required CI, current rebuilt real-provider validation or a complete R9 pass."
  ]
